doctor":0.11936}},{"id":"EDU-13","title":"Managing stress","text":"Stress is a normal response to pressure, but long periods of stress can affect sleep, mood and the body. Helpful habits include regular exercise, breaks, talking with someone you trust, and relaxation techniques such as slow breathing. Support is available from counsellors and doctors.","vec":{"manag":0.281974,"stres":0.443648,"normal":0.166539,"response":0.185915,"pressure":0.126047,"but":0.185915,"long":0.133414,"period":0.166539,"affect":0.185915,"sleep":0.142127,"mood":0.166539,"body":0.126047,"helpful":0.166539,"habit":0.152791,"include":0.152791,"regular":0.114038,"exercise":0.166539,"break":0.185915,"talk":0.152791,"someone":0.166539,"trust":0.185915,"relaxation":0.185915,"techniqu":0.185915,"such":0.109003,"slow":0.185915,"breath":0.166539,"support":0.114038,"available":0.185915,"counsellor":0.166539,"doctor":0.114038}},{"id":"EDU-14","title":"Vaccinations","text":"Vaccines train the immune system to recognise germs before you meet them. National schedules list recommended vaccines for babies, children and adults. Keeping a record of your vaccinations and asking your doctor which ones you may need is a useful habit.","vec":{"vaccination":0.356667,"vaccin":0.350141,"train":0.206799,"immune":0.185246,"system":0.185246,"recognise":0.206799,"germ":0.206799,"before":0.158092,"meet":0.206799,"national":0.206799,"schedul":0.206799,"list":0.158092,"recommend":0.185246,"baby":0.185246,"children":0.206799,"adult":0.158092,"keep":0.126847,"record":0.1484,"ask":0.158092,"doctor":0.126847,"one":0.169954,"may":0.206799,"need":0.126847,"useful":0.206799,"habit":0.169954}},{"id":"EDU-15","title":"Handwashing and infection prevention","text":"Washing hands with soap and water for about twenty seconds reduces the spread of many infections. Wash before eating or preparing food, after using the toilet, and after coughing or sneezing. Covering coughs and staying home when sick also helps protect others.","vec":{"